@startuml sequence-add-book
' BookCode — adding a book (uploading a PDF).
' IDs like (D13) or (P7) refer to the decision log in docs/architecture/README.md.

title Adding a book (upload → approval → processing)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
autonumber

actor "Uploader" as up
participant "React SPA" as spa
participant "Express API\n(IngestionService)" as api
participant "IngestionRunner\n(in-process, D12)" as runner
participant "ProgressEventBus\n(in-process, P14)" as bus
database "Temp PDF storage\n(local disk)" as disk
database "MongoDB" as db
participant "Gemini API\n(free tier, D17)" as gem

== 1. Upload ==
up -> spa : choose a PDF, click Upload
spa -> api : POST /api/ingestion-jobs\n(multipart: PDF)
activate api
api -> api : check it is a PDF; size limit (O4)
api -> disk : save PDF
api -> db : insert IngestionJob {status: DETECTING, uploaderId,\npdfPath, approvalDeadline: now + 24 h (D9)}
api ->> runner : detectMetadata(jobId)  [not awaited]
api --> spa : 202 Accepted {jobId}
deactivate api
spa -> spa : go to /upload/{jobId}  (P2: a refresh returns here)
spa -> api : GET /api/ingestion-jobs/{jobId}/events  (SSE)
api -> bus : subscribe(jobId)
note right of api
  On subscribe the API first sends the job's current state,
  so an event published before the browser connected isn't missed.
  Before approval only the uploader may subscribe;
  while PROCESSING any signed-in user may (P6).
end note

== 2. Detect title, authors and edition ==
activate runner
runner -> disk : read PDF
runner -> runner : cut out the first 15 pages (P7)
runner -> gem : generateContent(pages, "title, subtitle,\nauthors, edition number → JSON")
alt Gemini error
  gem --> runner : error
  runner -> db : job → FAILED (reason)
  runner -> disk : delete PDF
  runner -> bus : publish(failed)
  bus --> spa : event: failed
  spa --> up : "We couldn't read this PDF"
else Gemini responds
  gem --> runner : {mainTitle, fullTitle, authors, editionNumber}\n(any field may be missing — the uploader fills it in, P2)
  runner -> db : job → AWAITING_APPROVAL, detected = metadata
  runner -> bus : publish(metadataDetected)
  bus --> spa : event: metadataDetected
  spa --> up : approval form, pre-filled
end
deactivate runner

== 3. Approve (D8) ==
alt uploader cancels (P2)
  up -> spa : Cancel
  spa -> api : POST /api/ingestion-jobs/{jobId}/cancel
  api -> db : job → CANCELLED
  api -> disk : delete PDF
else uploader approves, after correcting any field (P2)
  up -> spa : Approve
  spa -> api : POST /api/ingestion-jobs/{jobId}/approve\n{mainTitle, fullTitle, authors, editionNumber}
  activate api
  api -> db : check job: belongs to this user,\nAWAITING_APPROVAL, before its deadline
  api -> api : normalise → matchKey (D7)
  api -> db : upsert Book by matchKey
  api -> db : atomic claim of Edition {bookId, editionNumber} (P3):\nset PROCESSING + lock {jobId, heartbeatAt: now}\nonly if it doesn't exist, is FAILED,\nor its lock is older than 10 min (D13, P4)
  alt edition is READY (D6)
    api -> db : job → REJECTED ("already processed")
    api -> disk : delete PDF
    api --> spa : 409 {editionId}
    spa --> up : "This edition is already on BookCode" + link
  else edition is PROCESSING with a fresh lock (D14)
    api -> db : job → REJECTED ("being processed")
    api -> disk : delete PDF
    api --> spa : 409
    spa --> up : "Someone is already processing this edition"
  else claimed
    api -> db : delete chapters + questions left by\nany earlier attempt (retry starts over, D13)
    api -> db : job → PROCESSING, editionId
    api ->> runner : process(jobId)  [not awaited]
    api --> spa : 202 {editionId}
    spa --> up : book page (work in progress)
  end
  deactivate api
end

== 4. Book page while processing — any signed-in user (D15, P6) ==
spa -> api : GET /api/editions/{editionId}
api --> spa : {status: PROCESSING, activeJobId, progress}\n(no questions until READY, D16)
spa -> api : GET /api/ingestion-jobs/{jobId}/events  (SSE)
api -> bus : subscribe(jobId)

== 5. Processing (inside the Express process, D12) ==
activate runner
runner -> disk : read PDF
runner -> gem : generateContent(whole PDF,\n"list chapters with page ranges → JSON")
gem --> runner : chapters
runner -> db : insert Chapters; progress.chaptersTotal
runner -> bus : publish(progress)
bus --> spa : event: progress

loop each chapter, one at a time (P7)
  runner -> db : refresh heartbeat — only if lock.jobId = this job (P4);\nif it isn't, stop: see "lock lost" below
  runner -> runner : cut out the chapter's pages
  runner -> gem : generateContent(chapter pages + instructions\n+ list of supported runtimes)
  note right of gem
    For each exercise: code or abstract; language + version;
    statement word for word; signature; starter code;
    harness (D23, P9); 2–3 visible + hidden tests (D24);
    "order doesn't matter" flag (D26).
  end note
  opt per-minute rate limit (HTTP 429)
    runner -> runner : wait, then resend the same request
  end
  gem --> runner : exercises (JSON)
  runner -> runner : discard: abstract (D20); language not supported (D21);\npinned version not supported (D22); malformed (P7).\nNo pinned version → latest supported (A5)
  runner -> db : insert Questions (hidden until the edition is READY)
  runner -> db : update job progress
  runner -> bus : publish(progress)
  bus --> spa : event: progress (e.g. chapter 4 of 12, 37 questions)
end

alt every chapter processed
  runner -> db : Edition → READY, readyAt; remove lock
  runner -> db : job → SUCCEEDED
  runner -> disk : delete PDF (D10)
  runner -> bus : publish(completed)
  bus --> spa : event: completed
  spa -> api : GET /api/editions/{editionId}
  api --> spa : chapters + questions
  spa --> up : questions can now be opened
else lock lost (another upload claimed the edition after 10 min without a heartbeat)
  runner -> db : job → FAILED ("lock lost")
  runner -> disk : delete PDF
  note right of runner
    Leaves the edition alone:
    it now belongs to the other job.
  end note
else daily quota used up, repeated unparseable output, or any other error (P5, P7)
  runner -> db : delete this edition's chapters + questions
  runner -> db : Edition → FAILED (reason); remove lock
  runner -> db : job → FAILED
  runner -> disk : delete PDF
  runner -> bus : publish(failed)
  bus --> spa : event: failed
  spa --> up : "Processing failed — upload the PDF again to retry"
end
deactivate runner

== Housekeeping (Start-up & sweeper tasks) ==
group every few minutes
  api -> db : jobs AWAITING_APPROVAL past their deadline → EXPIRED (D9)
  api -> disk : delete their PDFs
end
group when the API starts (P4)
  api -> db : jobs still PROCESSING → FAILED;\ntheir editions → FAILED, chapters + questions deleted
  api -> disk : delete their PDFs
end

@enduml
